   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">Dear all,</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><br></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">I just wanted to make sure about one thing whether my Stan\r\ncode is correct or not.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">It is just a basic question. Your help is greatly\r\nappreciated.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nx has a bivariate standard normal distribution.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">The limit state function (g(x)) works as a variable into the likelihood : <br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><br></span></p><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">likelihood </span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sqrt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\">pi</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> exp </span><span style=\"color:#660\">[(-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> g</span><span style=\"color:#660\">^</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">where</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> g </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sum</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sqrt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">and</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> the </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Gaussian</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> prior </span><span style=\"color:#008\">is</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> on x </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> x </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> normal </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)).</span></div></code></div><code><span style=\"line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><br></span></code><p></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><code><span style=\"line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">my Stan code:<br></span></code></span></p><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>parameters </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>transformed parameters </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>real g </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sum</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sqrt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">));</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>model </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">//Gaussian prior</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  x </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> normal</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">//likelihood </span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  g </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> normal</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><code><span style=\"line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><br></span></code></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><code><span style=\"line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">Is the above Stan code correct? <br></span></code></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">Thank you for your consideration.<br></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">Hamed</span></p>\r\n\r\n</div>"
