    [
     1,
     "The problem is that after i run it and printing out the results, the mean of g is 1.5 while in my likelihood function i defined it to be equal to 0.<br>and the generated bivariate x samples are as following which was centered at 1.1.  The red line is showing the g =0.<br><br><img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/stan-users/attach/7837ba4220241/Auto%20Generated%20Inline%20Image%201?part=0.1\" alt=\"\"><br>while it is supposed to be as following: (when g = 0, x1 and x2 is equal to 3/sqrt(2) )<br>because at g = 0 i defined my likelihood function to be maximum. ( the red line is showing the g = 0 )<br>( the vertical and horizontal axis are presenting the bivariate samples)<br><br><img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/stan-users/attach/7837ba4220241/Auto%20Generated%20Inline%20Image%202?part=0.2\" alt=\"\"><br>I would gratefully appreciate it if you could let me know where my mistake is.<br><br>Thank you very much for all your works and efforts.<br>Hamed"
    ],
